<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#caste">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Caste</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Caste refers to a system of hereditary social groups, often tied to occupation and restricting marriage between groups. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jolof-empire">Jolof Empire</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wolof">Wolof</a> society distinguished nobles, free commoners, artisan castes such as blacksmiths and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/griots">griots</a>, and enslaved people. The term is also used more loosely for hereditary social and occupational categories in other societies, including <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing China</a>.</p></div>
